/**

@page page_peano_runtime_analysis Runtime analysis

\tableofcontents

Peano applications report global grid, memory and rank-partition statistics
after every phase. The Grid Snapshot presents the latest synchronised view
across all ranks.

# Grid

The row `Cells` of the grid section reports the number of unrefined cells
with the refined cells above them in brackets, the row `Faces` the number of
faces with the hanging faces among them, and the row `Levels` the minimum and
maximum grid levels. These counts describe the global logical grid.

# MPI decomposition

The section appears with more than one rank; the configuration summary names
the number of ranks. `Load Balance` divides the average cell count of a rank
by the cell count of the most loaded rank and prints the minimum and maximum
cells per rank. `Rank Boundary Faces` gives the percentage of the faces two
ranks hold and their minimum and maximum per rank.

A low balance value identifies unequal ownership. Many rank-boundary faces
identify a small local workload relative to the halo traffic.

# Memory

`CPU Grid` and `GPU Grid` report the bytes of the partition and the tree in
host and device memory, `CPU Solver Data` and `GPU Solver Data` the bytes of
the application data, and `Used` the resident set of the process with the free
and the total memory of the node.

# Regridding

The dynamic-AMR report records the number of regrids and sweeps with their
wall clock, and the grid, MPI decomposition and memory rows before the first
and after the last regrid.

@ref page_peano_performance_optimisation provides tuning guidance.

*/
